# riboseq_signal_model -- what git tracks is the CODE and the WRITE-UP (~20 MB).
# The 3.5 TB of data, packs, checkpoints and search output stays on the group filesystem.
#
# Override for a specific file with `git add -f <path>` (e.g. a small test fixture).

# ---- bulk data: 3.5 TB, never in git ----
# Leading slash ANCHORS these to the repo root. Without it, `data/` also matches
# tutorial/source/data (tutorial prose, 5.5 KB) and any other nested dir of that name.
/data/
/results/
/proteogenomics/data/

# ---- SLURM stdout/stderr ----
# 2,255 files / 17 MB that churn on every run. They REMAIN ON DISK as the project's run
# record (the logs/ rule in CLAUDE.md is about keeping them, not about tracking them);
# tracking them would make `git status` and every diff unreadable.
# To include them instead, delete these two lines.
*.out
*.err

# ---- Sphinx build artifacts (regenerate: cd tutorial && make html) ----
tutorial/build/
tutorial/index.html
**/.doctrees/

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- large/regenerable binaries (belt-and-braces; the dirs above already cover these) ----
*.pt
*.pth
*.npy
*.npz
*.hd5
*.h5
*.bam
*.bai
*.bed
*.fastq
*.fq
*.mzML
*.mzBIN*
*.pepXML
*.pin
*.gz
*.sif

# ---- editor / OS ----
.DS_Store
*.swp

# One-off junk: a PRICE invocation with an unexpanded ${prefix} shell variable wrote these
# two files literally named "${prefix}.*" (2026-07-18). Left on disk, not tracked.
${prefix}.*

# EXCEPTIONS force-added with `git add -f` (git cannot re-include a file whose parent dir is
# excluded, so these are tracked explicitly rather than via a negation pattern):
#   data/packed_union/NAMING_WARNING.md      -- the bare-name/nokozak-content hazard
#   data/packed_union/orf_track_v2_meta.json -- authoritative kozak setting for the released models

# ---- other run logs ----
# Same rule as the SLURM *.out/*.err above: fetch logs, adapter checks and Sphinx build output are
# the on-disk run record, not repo content. They churn and would drown every diff.
*.log

# ---- plan/document backups ----
# CLAUDE.md requires a timestamped backup before overwriting a plan. Those live next to the original
# on disk; the repo keeps the current version and git keeps the history.
*.bak
*.bak.*

# Bundle tarballs are build products of deliverables/<name>/; the directory is tracked.
deliverables/*.tar.gz
